## User preferences

- when review should “no longer be on request” and happen “in editor ... as a person is saving” -> default editor AI to quiet saved-draft/idle processing, not isolated manual tools [Task 1]
- when asking whether features are “implemented in editor” -> verify real editor event wiring and visible in-editor output, not only a standalone route or panel [Task 1]
- when styling should be “consistent with our other styles” -> reuse Twyne tokens, shared controls, typography, and Editorial Board vocabulary rather than a local styling system [Task 1]
- when the user authorized “Configure the integration” -> provision and verify the live provider boundary rather than stopping at source code [Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- `src/utils/live-review.ts` owns saved-draft review, persistence by folio, retry/backoff, and `twyne:live-review` / `twyne:quick-review`; `src/components/writing-tools/live-review-status.tsx` provides status, findings, pause/resume, and unavailable-state routing. Preserve typed findings, uncertainty, evidence passages, and read-only behavior: review must not edit prose automatically. [Task 1]
- Background work needs spend guards: substantive word threshold, idle delay, minimum interval, and per-session cap. TypeSafe calls use typed `state` plus `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; Choice has a criteria map, Score ordered levels, and Noul has no confidence. [Task 1]
- Not Organic production uses `https://api.notorganic.info`, capability `judgement:evaluate`, and DPoP-bound tokens. Link with PKCE one-time state and server-side token/account verification; do not trust a browser-supplied DID, expose gateway credentials, or send upstream error bodies to browsers. [Task 2]

